{{also|bulle|bullé}}
==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbʊlə/|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably a [[pars pro toto]] expression, from a very old root (related to Ancient Greek {{term|φαλλός||penis|tr=phallos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}), with the related meaning "ball".

====Noun====
{{de-noun|g=m|genitive=Bullen|plural=Bullen}}

# [[bull|Bull]] (male cattle).

===Etymology 2===
Since the 19th century documented; the colloquial (or possibly baby talk) abbreviation ''Pole'' gets in dialects having lenition of consonants as well as ''o/u''-concurrence homonymous with [[#Etymology_1|Bulle]] and generally established because of the obvious association. Another source is suggesting that it derived from ''(Land)Puller'', a non-derogatory term for a policeman of the 18th century.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|g=m|genitive=Bullen|plural=Bullen}}

# (derogatory) Male [[cop]].

=====Related terms=====
* [[Bullette]]

===Etymology 3===
From {{etyl|la|de}} ''[[bulla]]'' "seal capsule", originally meaning "ball, bullet".

====Noun====
{{de-noun|g=f|plural=Bullen}}

# [[bull|Bull]] (papal decree).

=====Related terms=====
* [[Bulette]]

